   105	patients in the FDOPA\_01 dataset were antipsychotic naïve (no current or previous treatment) or free (not taking medication at scanning time with at least 6 months washout for oral medication or 6 months for depot medication) [7]. The FDOPA\_02 dataset included patients with a DSM-IV diagnosis of SCZ [45]. Patients in the FDOPA\_03 dataset were also patients who met the DSM-IV criteria for SCZ, paranoid subtype. All patients were taking antipsychotic medication at the time of scanning other than clozapine [9]. Lastly, the FDOPA\_04 dataset included patients who met the DSM-V criteria for SCZ or schizophreniform disorders [46]. Also, in the FDOPA\_04 dataset all patients were taking antipsychotic medication at the time of scanning other than clozapine. Full information on the recruitment criteria and clinical characteristics of the patient population is reported in the original papers [7, 13, 14, 42 -48]. For a subset of patients of the FDOPA\_01 and FDOPA\_04 datasets, symptom severity measures (i.e., Positive and Negative Symptoms Scale -PANSS [51]) were also available.
